      "additions": 30,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/58868cc3f554d2d1f9ad2bb69410ac44951a0a3e/docs%2Fdocs%2Fadvanced_features%2Ftool_parser.mdx",
      "changes": 30,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/docs%2Fdocs%2Fadvanced_features%2Ftool_parser.mdx?ref=58868cc3f554d2d1f9ad2bb69410ac44951a0a3e",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "docs/docs/advanced_features/tool_parser.mdx",
      "patch": "@@ -118,6 +118,36 @@ wait_for_server(f\"http://localhost:{port}\")\n \n Note that `--tool-call-parser` defines the parser used to interpret responses.\n \n+### Unknown tool names in agent loops\n+\n+The model can emit a tool name that is not in the request's `tools` list. If the\n+parser removes that call, your agent may receive no `tool_calls` and treat the\n+turn as complete instead of giving the model a chance to correct the name.\n+\n+[`SGLANG_FORWARD_UNKNOWN_TOOLS`](/docs/references/environment_variables) controls\n+whether parsers that support this setting forward unknown calls. The default is\n+`false`. To enable forwarding, set it in the server process's environment before\n+starting the server. For example, in a POSIX shell on Linux:\n+\n+```bash\n+export SGLANG_FORWARD_UNKNOWN_TOOLS=1\n+```\n+\n+Then use the launch command appropriate for your model and hardware. Set the\n+variable to `0` to disable forwarding in parsers that honor it.\n+\n+Your client must still validate each tool name before execution. For an unknown\n+name, append the assistant's tool-call message to the conversation, return an\n+error as a `role=\"tool\"` message with the matching `tool_call_id`, and request\n+another model turn. Include the supported tool names in the error so the model\n+can retry with an available tool.\n+\n+Support varies by parser and request mode. For example, `mimo` honors the setting\n+in non-streaming mode, while the shared JSON streaming path used by `qwen25`\n+currently drops unknown names even when forwarding is enabled. Test the parser\n+and streaming mode you deploy; enabling the variable alone does not guarantee\n+that every parser will forward unknown calls.\n+\n \n ### Define Tools for Function Call\n Below is a Python snippet that shows how to define a tool as a dictionary. The dictionary includes a tool name, a description, and property defined Parameters.",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/58868cc3f554d2d1f9ad2bb69410ac44951a0a3e/docs%2Fdocs%2Fadvanced_features%2Ftool_parser.mdx",
